In this work, we synthesized a novel Ru-MOF nanosheets (RuMOFNSs) by a simple one-pot method based on the cooperative self-assembly reaction of \(\mathrm{Zn}^{2+}\) and \(\mathrm{Ru}(\mathrm{dcbpy})_{3}^{2+}\) as organic ligands. \(\mathrm{Ru}(\mathrm{dcbpy})_{3}^{2+}\) are water-soluble, making it

possible to synthesize MOFs in aqueous phase and avoiding environmental pollution caused by organic solvents. The highly exposed \(\mathrm{Ru}(\mathrm{dcbpy})_{3}^{2+}\) reactive sites, large surface area and abundant functionalized groups of the synthesized RuMOFNSs are expected to enhance ECL efficiency and to facilitate the loading of antibodies for immunoassay. Therefore, a cathode ECL immunosensor was proposed with the RuMOFNSs as signal probe for the determination of cTnI, an important biomarker of acute myocardial infarction (AMI).37-39 Scheme 1 briefly summarized the preparation process of RuMOFNSs and the assembly process of immunosensor. This sensing platform exhibited excellent analytical performance for the detection of cTnI, which held great application prospect for target proteins detection in clinical analysis.

