# EXPERIMENTAL SECTION

Chemicals and Materials. Zinc nitrate hexahydrate \(\left(\mathrm{Zn}(\mathrm{NO}_{3})_{2}{\cdot}6\mathrm{H}_{2}\mathrm{O}\right.\), \(99\%\) ) was gained from J&K Scientific Ltd.(Beijing, China). 1-ethyl-3-[3-(dimethylamino)-propyl] carbodiimide hydrochloride (EDC), N-hydroxysuccinimide (NHS), Polyvinylpyrrolidone (PVP, \(\mathrm{Mw}{=}40{,}000\)), Pyrazine \((99\%)\) and albumin from bovine serum (BSA) were purchased from Sigma-Aldrich. Tris (4,4'-dicarboxylicacid-2,2'-bipyridyl) ruthenium(II) dichloride \(\left(\mathrm{Ru}(\mathrm{dcbpy})_{3}^{2+}\right)\) was acquired from Suna Tech Inc (Suzhou, China). Other reagents were bought from Beijing Chemical Reagent Company (Beijing, China). Phosphate buffer solution a (PBSa, pH 7.4, 0.1 M) and washing buffer solution (PBSb, pH 7.4, 0.01 M) were prepared using \(\mathrm{Na}_{2}\mathrm{HPO}_{4}\) and \(\mathrm{NaH}_{2}\mathrm{PO}_{4}\). The cardiac troponin (cTnI, cTnT and cTnC), anti-alpha fetoprotein (AFP) polyclonal antibody (rabbit, Ab1), anti-cTnI monoclonal antibody (mouse, mAb) and polyclonal antibody (rabbit, pAb) were purchased form Abcam (Cambridge, MA). The human plasma was kindly supplied by the Second Hospital of Jilin University (Changchun, China). Unless otherwise specified, other reagents were of analytical grade and were used without further purification. Ultrapure water (18.2 MΩ cm) from a Millipore system was used in all aqueous solutions.

\(\mathrm{Ab}_{1}\)), anti-cTnI monoclonal antibody (mouse, mAb) and polyclonal antibody (rabbit, pAb) were purchased form Abcam (Cambridge, MA). The human plasma was kindly supplied by the Second Hospital of Jilin University (Changchun, China). Unless otherwise specified, other reagents were of analytical grade and were used without further purification. Ultrapure water ( \(18.2\ \mathrm{M}\Omega\ \mathrm{cm})\) from a Millipore system was used in all aqueous solutions.

Apparatus. Transmission electron microscope (TEM), the scanning TEM (STEM) and the elemental mapping measurements of RuMOFNSs were acquired with a Tecnai G2 F20 S-TWIN electron microscope (FEI, American) and the accelerating voltage was \(200\ \mathrm{kV}\). Scanning electron microscope (SEM) images and energy dispersive X-ray spectroscopy (EDX) analysis were executed on a XL30 ESEM FEG microscope with an accelerating voltage of 20
kV. X-ray photoelectron spectroscopy (XPS) measurements were performed on an ESCALABMK II (VG Scientific) with Al Kα as the exciting source. X-ray powder diffraction (XRD) patterns were recorded with a D8-Advance system (Bruker, Germany) with Cu Kα radiation \((\lambda{=}1.5406\mathring{\mathrm{A}})\). UV-vis absorption characterization was performed on a CARY 50 Scan UV-vis spectrometer (Varian, USA). Atomic force microscopy (AFM) image was measured by Dimension Icon SPM (Bruker, Germany). FT-IR spectra were measured by Bruker VERTEX70 spectrometer (Ettlingen, Germany). ECL measurements were performed using MPI-E ECL analytical system (Xi'an Remex, China). The potential ranges from 0.00 to \(-1.60\,\mathrm{~V~}\) for cathodic scanning, with a scan rate of \(100~\mathrm{\mV/s}\), and photomultiplier tube (PMT) voltage of \(450\ \mathrm{~V~}\). The electrochemical and ECL measurements were performed with a three-electrode system, composing of \(\mathrm{Ag/AgCl}\) reference electrode, platinum wire counter electrodes, and bare or modified glassy carbon electrode (GCE, \(\mathrm{d}{=}3\mathrm{~\mm}\)) as working electrode. The electrolyte for ECL detection was PBSa solution \((3\,\mathrm{\mL})\) containing \(0.1\,\mathrm{~M~KCl}\), and \(0.1\,\mathrm{~M~K}_{2}\mathrm{S}_{2}\mathrm{O}_{8}\) was added in the electrolyte as co-reactant.

Preparation of RuMOFNSs. \(\mathrm{Zn}(\mathrm{NO}_{3})_{2}\cdot6\mathrm{H}_{2}\mathrm{O}\) \((9.0\,\mathrm{mg})\), PVP \((20~\mathrm{mg})\), \(\mathrm{Ru}(\mathrm{dcbpy})_{3}{}^{2+}\) \((9.0~\mathrm{mg})\) and pyrazine \((1.6~\mathrm{mg})\) were dissolved with \(32\,\textrm{m L}\) \(\mathrm{H}_{2}\mathrm{O}\) in a \(50\,\textrm{m L}\) round flask. After that, the solution was sonicated for \(5~\mathrm{min}\) to obtain a homogeneous solution. Then the flask was heated to \(80~^{\circ}\mathrm{C}\) and kept for \(24\,\mathrm{~h~}\). The resulting orange crystals were centrifuged \((12000\,\mathrm{\rpm}\), \(10\,\mathrm{\min})\) and thoroughly washed

three times with DI water. The obtained RuMOFNSs were eventually redispersed into water \((0.24\;\mathrm{mg/mL})\).

Modification of RuMOFNSs with Antibody. The as-prepared RuMOFNSs solution \((1\ \mathrm{mL},\,0.24\ \mathrm{mg/mL})\) was activated by \(200\,\upmu\mathrm{L}\) mixture solution of EDC/NHS (400 \(\mathrm{mM}/100\ \mathrm{mM}\) ) under the gently stirring at room temperature (RT) for \(2~\mathrm{h}\), followed by adding \(10~\upmu\mathrm{L}\) of pAb \((1~\mathrm{mg/mL})\) and stirring overnight at \(4~^{\circ}\mathrm{C}\). Subsequently, the resulting RuMOFNSs-pAb bioconjugate was collected by centrifugal washing \((12000\ \mathrm{rpm}\), \(10\ \mathrm{min})\) with PBSb twice to remove free antibody. Finally, the RuMOFNSs-pAb was redispersed in \(1\,\textrm{m L}\) PBSb containing \(1\%\) BSA for \(1\,\mathrm{~h~}\) to block the excess binding sites. After centrifugal washing, the resultant signal probe was dispersed with \(1\mathrm{mL}\) PBSb and stored at \(4\,^{\circ}\mathrm{C}\) for later use.

Fabrication of ECL immunosensor. The bare GCE was pretreated and electrodeposited a thin layer of Au NPs according to the reported literature.40 Initially, the Au NPs modified GCE was incubated with \(8~\upmu\mathrm{L}\) of mAb \((10~\upmu\mathrm{g/mL})\) for \(12\,\mathrm{~h~}\) at \(4~^{\circ}\mathrm{C}\) to absorb mAb onto the Au NPs layer. Thereafter, \(4~\upmu\mathrm{L}\) of BSA \((1\%)\) solution was placed onto the electrode for 1h at RT to block the nonspecific adsorption sites. Next, the modified electrode mAb/Au NP/GCE was incubated with \(10~\upmu\mathrm{L}\) of cTnI antigen \((\mathrm{Ag})\) with a series of different concentrations and kept for \(90\,\mathrm{\min}\), followed by further incubated with the RuMOFNSs-pAb bioconjugate for \(1\ \mathrm{~h~}\). The sandwiched type ECL immunosensor was fabricated by immunological recognition. After each modification step, the electrode was softly rinsed with 3-fold volume PBSb to remove weakly-bound components.

